<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">State of the Presidi</h1><p class="st-meta">1557 CE – 1801 CE · capital Orbetello</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A string of Spanish-held fortresses on the Tuscan coast that let Spain and later Naples watch over central Italy for nearly 250 years.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a> granted the conquered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-siena">Republic of Siena</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici">Cosimo I de' Medici</a> in 1557, he kept the coastal fortresses of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orbetello">Orbetello</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto-ercole">Porto Ercole</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talamone">Talamone</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto-santo-stefano">Porto Santo Stefano</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ansedonia">Ansedonia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto-longone">Porto Longone</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elba">Elba</a> was added in 1603.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Presidi, meaning garrisons, were run as a military district under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-naples">Kingdom of Naples</a>. Their purpose was strategic: to secure Spanish sea routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-genoa">Genoa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> and to watch the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-tuscany">Grand Duchy of Tuscany</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> built powerful fortifications at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto-ercole">Porto Ercole</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orbetello">Orbetello</a>. The painter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravaggio">Caravaggio</a> died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto">Porto</a> Ercole in 1610.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Presidi passed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in 1707 and to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbons</a> in 1735. In 1801 the Treaty of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-florence">Florence</a> ceded them to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, which joined them to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-etruria">Kingdom of Etruria</a>; after 1815 they became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-tuscany">Tuscany</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/state-of-the-presidi.jpg" alt="State of the Presidi" width="320" height="494"><figcaption>Image: Robert Wilkinson, London, 1800. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tuscany,_Piombino,_Elba,_State_of_the_Presidios,_1800.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1557 CE – 1801 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Orbetello</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Philip II of Spain</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian, Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Stato dei Presidi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1679&amp;focus=state-of-the-presidi" aria-label="State of the Presidi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4952 669 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where State of the Presidi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5272 925L4910 989M5272 925L5349 976M5272 925L5270 883"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4910 989h0M5349 976h0M5270 883h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d